      "conclusion": "partial",
      "summary": "Over the last hour (2026-10-22T15:17:35Z–16:17:35Z) the recommendation service shows steady span volume, no error status on its own server spans, latency comparable to the prior hour, and very low CPU/memory usage on a single healthy replica. The only error-status series present is a recurring client span to flagd's EventStream, and its counter advanced at the same rate in the preceding hour, so it is a steady background pattern rather than a new fault. Resource headroom is large (container CPU averaged ~0.009 cores, working set ~46 MB against a 500 MiB limit, zero memory pressure waiting) and the pod did not restart during the hour. However, a full 'healthy' verdict is not established: the service exposes no non-trace error-rate counter, no logs or span error details were available to explain the flagd errors, no latency SLO or alert state was provided, and the trace view is only a 4-trace sample. One internal inconsistency (stepped error increases reporting zero while the raw counter stepped +6) also limits confidence in the error timing.",
